  {
   "id": 6,
   "parent": 5,
   "node_type": "proof",
   "text": "\\begin{proof}\nEach token contributes one key and one value, which gives the factor $2$.\nIn one layer a key holds $N_{KV}$ heads of $d_{\\text{head}}$ numbers, so it has $N_{KV} d_{\\text{head}}$ numbers, and so does a value.\nEvery layer stores its own pair, which multiplies by $N_{\\text{layers}}$, and every number takes $b$ bytes.\nMultiplying over $L$ tokens gives the formula.\n\\end{proof}\n\n",
